	(text "Pad order: 1 VIN, 2 GND, 3 SWDCLK, 4 SWDIO, 5 UART_RX, 6 UART_TX.\n- TVS at the pad on VIN (D601) and on each data pad (D602-D605). No TVS on pad 2: it is the GND reference.\n  D601 replaces the VIN TVS that was on the power sheet (the pads and the PMIC are on different islands).\n- 100 ohm in series between each data pad and the SoC net (R601-R604), TVS on the pad side.\n- R605 100k pull-down on UART_RX at the SoC side, so the RX input does not float off the dock.\n- Firmware enables the UART only while the PMIC reports VBUS present.\n- SWDIO has an always-on internal pull-up in the nRF54L15, so pad 4 sits at 1.8 V on the skin all night.\n- Pads: ENIG for rev A (JLCPCB flex); hard gold (PCBWay) if pogo wear shows."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1c2b651a-5538-42fc-b5e5-9a58ecb712cd")
	)
	(text "Dock sheet (step 6): six pogo pads on the skin face of island B, 2 mm pitch, 1.2 x 3.0 mm each (J601 footprint)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2558cf70-cefe-411d-8d1f-cca36d43720f")
	)
	(text "(check):\n- TPD1E10B06DPYR: Vrwm 5.5 V (bidirectional), clamp 10 V at 1 A, C 12 pF. Leakage is 100 nA MAX at 5 V, above the\n  50 nA target. For VIN this does not matter (0 V off the dock). For the four 1.8 V data pads the datasheet gives\n  no figure at 1.8 V: measure it, or pick a part with a guaranteed low leakage at 1.8 V.\n- TVS footprint: KiCad D_0402 used for TI's DPY (X1SON 1.0 x 0.6 mm); check against TI's land pattern."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 208.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ff8bc121-9dbb-4c9f-8301-42dc9ae158b8")
	)
